  "caption": "Quinn joined the social volleyball team, jumped for every ball, then landed on a teammate's foot and rolled an ankle. Knees and shoulder were grumbling too.\n\nVolleyball tends to cause two kinds of trouble: sudden ankle sprains when landing near the net, and slower overuse of knees and shoulders from lots of jumping and swinging.\n\nWhat can help: balance training (especially after a past sprain), a brace on top of rehab — braces don't weaken the ankle — counting weekly jumps in preseason and building gradually, and treating serving and spiking as shoulder load, with good net spacing.\n\nGet it checked if you can't take a few steps, a shoulder dislocates, muscle wastes around the shoulder blade, or a finger won't straighten.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
